@startuml order-status
!include ../_theme.puml
title Order lifecycle (OrderStatusPolicy)

' Derived from: wovely services/OrderStatusPolicy, OrderService#transition / #applyIntervention
hide empty description

[*] --> PENDING : checkout\n(stock deducted)
PENDING --> CONFIRMED : seller
PENDING --> PROCESSING : seller
CONFIRMED --> PROCESSING : seller
PROCESSING --> SHIPPED : seller\n[tracking number set]
SHIPPED --> DELIVERED : buyer confirms receipt\nor seller
DELIVERED --> COMPLETED : buyer / seller

PENDING --> CANCELLED : buyer / seller\n<<restock>>
CONFIRMED --> CANCELLED : buyer / seller\n<<restock>>
PROCESSING --> CANCELLED : seller\n<<restock>>

DELIVERED --> REFUNDED : all items returned\n(system, via ReturnService)
SHIPPED --> DISPUTED : admin MARK_DISPUTED
DELIVERED --> DISPUTED : admin MARK_DISPUTED
DISPUTED --> SHIPPED : admin RESOLVE_DISPUTE
DISPUTED --> DELIVERED : admin RESOLVE_DISPUTE
DISPUTED --> REFUNDED : admin FORCE_REFUND

state "Manual order" as MANUAL
[*] --> MANUAL : seller, off-platform sale
MANUAL --> COMPLETED : immediately

CANCELLED --> [*]
REFUNDED --> [*]

note right of PROCESSING
  Items/address editable only in
  PENDING and CONFIRMED (else 409).
  Edits reconcile stock per product.
  "Ship with Wovely" label (CONFIRMED /
  PROCESSING, once; admin may regenerate)
  sets carrier, CO₂ estimate and tracking.
end note

note bottom of REFUNDED
  CANCELLED and REFUNDED are terminal for everyone (409).
  Admins may force any other transition (UPDATE_STATUS,
  FORCE_REFUND, CANCEL_ORDER) — every intervention is audited.
  Restock happens only if the goods never shipped
  (from PENDING / CONFIRMED / PROCESSING).
  Wallet escrow: checkout debits the buyer; COMPLETED pays the
  seller; CANCELLED / REFUNDED / returns refund the buyer
  (reversing the payout if the seller was already paid).
end note
@enduml
